note array_bool.om: a bool ARRAY field. OMEGESE 9.4 says an array is never bool, so the compiler
note may either refuse this program (non-zero status, error text, no object) or run it correctly.
note It must not accept it and emit a program that dies by SIGILL. If it runs: true false true
note read back as 1 + 0 + 4 = 5.
struct Q v bool 3 end
fn main to uint
q = new Q true
put q v 1 false
r = uint 0
if eq get q v 0 true
r = add r 1
end
if eq get q v 1 true
r = add r 2
end
if eq get q v 2 true
r = add r 4
end
ret r
end
